<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Dadiani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century–1867</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Dadiani of Mingrelia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Dadiani was the Georgian princely family that ruled Mingrelia in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Nominal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the kings of Imereti, they were often stronger than their overlords and dominated neighbours such as Abkhazia and Svaneti. Mingrelia accepted Russian protection in 1803, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> abolished the principality in 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-dadiani.jpg" alt="House of Dadiani" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadezhda Abashvili · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerb_Dadianovii.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
